{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Therefore, you tax</b> (בושסכם) — it has no companion root [word], for the bet is a root letter, for it cannot be a servant [letter] with a verb [noun], except [if] its form and meaning [are] to do violence to the poor." "<b>And the levy of grain</b> — one who toiled for it, you take from him by force. And this is your recompense: houses of hewn stone you built."], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "The argument turns on whether bet in בושסכם is radical or servile; 'verb' here renders שם הפועל, lit. 'name of the actor/doing.' The clause after 'except' is elliptical and I translate it hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:18:08.635793941Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}